---
import ProviderPlaybookTemplate from '../components/ProviderPlaybookTemplate.astro';
const data = {
 "kind": "manage",
 "name": "Plesk",
 "title": "How to Add and Manage DNS Records in Plesk",
 "description": "Add, edit, and delete DNS records in Plesk step by step, with the gotchas that break sites and mail, and free tools to verify every change.",
 "intro": "Managing DNS in Plesk is a short walk once you know where the records live and which defaults to watch. This is the complete flow, with the verification step most guides skip.",
 "panel": "Plesk panel, Websites & Domains, the domain, DNS Settings (or the DNS section per subscription). Plesk runs the zone when DNS is enabled for the subscription.",
 "steps": [
  [
   "Open DNS Settings",
   "Websites & Domains, the domain, DNS Settings."
  ],
  [
   "Add the record",
   "Add Record: type, domain name, value. OK, then Update to apply."
  ],
  [
   "Template awareness",
   "Changes apply to the domain's zone; the DNS template only affects NEW domains."
  ],
  [
   "Verify",
   "Record lookup after saving; confirm the record with its TTL."
  ]
 ],
 "quirk": "Plesk can disable its DNS per domain (Tools, DNS Settings, Disable). When disabled, the panel still shows the template records, which do nothing: the classic Plesk trap.",
  "fieldMap": { "name": "Record name", "value": "Value", "ttl": "Default 86400 s", "apex": "Full domain with trailing dot", "note": "Plesk DNS settings usually sit under Websites & Domains, DNS. Default TTLs are higher than most cloud panels." },
"faqs": [
  [
   "Should Plesk or Cloudflare hold DNS?",
   "External anycast DNS (Cloudflare etc.) is more resilient than a single hosting server; keep Plesk DNS only for simplicity's sake."
  ],
  [
   "How long do DNS changes take in Plesk?",
   "The provider serves new values quickly, but resolvers keep old answers until each record's TTL expires. Verify live values with the record lookup, then watch the propagation checker until resolvers agree."
  ],
  [
   "Where do I find Plesk's nameservers?",
   "This playbook's nameservers guide covers the exact location. They are the delegation pair your registrar must point at for Plesk to be authoritative."
  ],
  [
   "Should I lower TTL before changing records in Plesk?",
   "Yes, for anything planned: set TTL to 300 seconds at least one old-TTL cycle ahead, make the change, confirm propagation, then restore the TTL."
  ],
  [
   "Can I keep email with one provider and DNS in Plesk?",
   "Yes: DNS host and mail provider are independent. Publish the mail provider's MX, SPF, DKIM, and DMARC records in Plesk, and keep those records unproxied."
  ],
  [
   "Which records should every domain have?",
   "A (and ideally AAAA) for the website, MX plus SPF/DKIM/DMARC for mail, and CAA to restrict certificate issuance. Everything else is per-service."
  ]
 ],
 "related": [
  [
   "DNS record types reference",
   "/dns-records/"
  ],
  [
   "TTL explained",
   "/what-is-ttl-in-dns/"
  ]
 ]
};
---
<ProviderPlaybookTemplate data={data} />
